From c2162344ccda3e6c03f2a763f13e05d10f85c6e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:17:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v2.3.3: de-cloud the browser surface, QoS imq0 gate,
 rexport + rmcpd hardening

DE-CLOUD (BACKLOG [P3]) - every remaining browser->ASUS-CDN request is gone from
the files that ship on this model. Verified against the staged fs.install tree,
not just source: several sites the source grep flagged are already inert inside
/* */ blocks that survive the build minifier.

- client_function.js x2 (productIcons): leaked the name of every ASUS-made LAN
  device from the admin browser and wrote the fetched icon into custom_usericon.
  v2.2.0/v2.2.5 closed the UI4 dashboard copy - which does not even ship - and
  missed this one, which 49 shipped pages load. Stub + guarded caller removed.
- adguard_dns.html: the AdGuard promo banner was fetched from the ASUS CDN with
  the BUNDLED copy wired only as an .on('error') fallback, so every visit to that
  page announced itself before quietly falling back. Now uses images/adGuard/
  directly. Found only by grepping the BUILT filesystem: an earlier pass decided
  which sysdep overlays ship by looking for a directory named after the overlay
  under fs.install, but the build copies overlay CONTENTS into the web root, so
  the directory never appears and every overlay looked non-shipping.
- collected_FAQ (form.js, reached from 31 pages), DNS_List x3 (System, WANPort,
  sdn.js), extend_sdn_scenarios, ui-model-name, extend_model_icon, tz_db,
  pppIspList_V2: the bundled /ajax/ copy is authoritative, cloud compare dropped.
- GameProfile.asp fetched gameProfile.json from ASUS and, on failure, re-armed
  itself every 5s forever. Now reads a bundled empty catalogue, no retry loop.
- Open NAT + IPTV profile feeds and the VPN partner server lists resolve locally;
  the surrounding UI still builds from an empty set.
- Per-game artwork REMOVED outright (104 .game-p-<name> rules, 414 lines). The
  images were publisher-owned game art hosted by ASUS - not ours to re-host in a
  redistributed image - and after the CDN urls were dropped every rule pointed at
  the same bundled placeholder anyway. The placeholder now lives on .game-profile
  and .new-g-p-image; the 4 structural .game-p-* rules are kept.
  NordVPN/Surfshark and CyberGhost promo banners no longer fetch.
- js/searchIspNameProfile.js deleted - 0 shipped pages included it.
- MULTISERVICE_WAN overlay: two dead /* */ blocks still carried CDN urls; the
  base file was already cleaned but the overlay is what actually ships.

DEAD CODE - the gated banner block, the empty icon stub and its caller, three
upstream /* */ blocks still carrying CDN urls, and the unreachable tail of the
v2.2.0 clientlist stub. Each proved unreachable AND orphan-free before cutting:
the naive scan called the banner block unsafe because six of its vars looked
live, but var hoisting was feeding an already-commented-out reader.

QOS - add_qos_rules() emitted the imq0 ingress redirect for the HARDWARE engines,
gated only on qos_irates (stock default non-zero), so it fired for qos_type 11 on
every apply: metal showed 4,619 pkts through imq0 with qos_ibw EMPTY and
qos_ipolicer=0. Only the tc/HTB engine builds an imq0 qdisc, so the redirect can
never shape anything. Corrects the [P2] backlog entry - its stated trigger
(qos_ibw > 0) and line reference (~2960) were both wrong.

REXPORT - the [P3] audit item is CLEAN: rexport_gen() emits a constant script and
every nvram read is quoted, so there is no shell injection. The exposure is one
layer over - values land in a curl -K config as url = "<value>", where a double
quote closes the string and the remainder is read as further curl directives;
`output = <path>` is an arbitrary file write as root. httpd stored url/token/
index/source/engine/metrics unvalidated. Added rexport_val_ok() + a runtime
guard in the generated script.

RMCPD - sb_scrub_secrets() only matched "<frag>[:=] value", so ASUS '>'-delimited
security tuples (apg1_security = <3>psk2>aes>PASSPHRASE>1) walked through the
structural scrub and a live PSK reached an operator transcript via the lab exec
tool. sb_scrub_sec_tuples() now runs first.

RWATCH - the armed log line hardcoded /jffs/rwatch even when rwatch_gen()
relocates DUMPROOT onto the durable store; it sent a live investigation to the
wrong path while the mirror was on the USB the whole time.

ALSO CARRIED (pre-existing uncommitted, inert): v2.3.3 Native Firewall Phase 1
scaffolding. reaper_fw.c is NOT referenced by rc/Makefile so nothing compiles,
Reaper_Firewall.asp is unwired, reaper_fw_enable defaults to 0.

NOT metal-validated. Verified against the staged filesystem after the build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
